"""
Template for smbios.local.py -- copy this file to smbios.local.py and fill in
values generated for YOUR machine:

    cp smbios.local.py.example smbios.local.py

Why this is not committed:  these four values are the identity macOS presents
to Apple ("which Mac am I").  If two machines present the same SystemSerialNumber
and MLB, Apple can flag both, and iMessage / FaceTime / App Store sign-in break
on each of them.  Never reuse a set you found on the internet -- including any
set that may appear in this repository's history.

How to generate:

  1. Get GenSMBIOS from https://github.com/corpnewt/GenSMBIOS
  2. Run it, choose "Generate SMBIOS", and enter:  MacBookPro15,2
     (see the SMBIOS comment in mkconfig.py for why 15,2 specifically)
  3. Copy the Serial and Board Serial (MLB) it prints below.
  4. SystemUUID: any random UUID.  `uuidgen` on macOS/Linux.
  5. ROM: 6 bytes as 12 hex characters.  Convention is your real built-in
     Ethernet/Wi-Fi MAC address with the colons removed, e.g. a MAC of
     00:11:22:aa:bb:cc becomes "001122AABBCC".  Any stable 12 hex chars work.

Do not add the values to this .example file -- put them in smbios.local.py.
"""
SystemSerialNumber = "PUT-YOUR-SERIAL-HERE"      # e.g. "C02XXXXXXXXX"
MLB                = "PUT-YOUR-MLB-HERE"         # e.g. "C02XXXXXXXXXXXXXX"
SystemUUID         = "PUT-YOUR-UUID-HERE"        # e.g. `uuidgen` output
ROM                = "PUTYOURROMHERE"            # 12 hex chars, no separators
